l_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"private","forks":0,"open_issues":9,"watchers":0,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"body":"### Project, step, and reason\n\nNon-blocking finding from G6c's round 2 review (#28, landed as 107e027), in 05_Agents/handoffs/2026-10-27-codex-to-claude-workflow-g6c-board-add-race-review-2.md.\n\n### What changes\n\ntools/workflow/issue.py, in open_issue: each planned step is a two-element list. The loop reads step[0] for the description and calls step[1], and the board step's add() rewrites step[0] through a closure over a variable assigned after add() is defined. The behaviour is correct, but the index arithmetic hides what each step holds. A small named type with description and action fields would say the same thing plainly. The same review also noted that board_card stops at the first malformed card, even when a valid card on the configured board comes later in the list. It judged that strict check defensible, so it is not part of this change.\n\n### Done when\n\nPlanned steps are a named type with description and action fields, open_issue reads no step by index, and the existing open tests pass unchanged.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sh4i-yurei/claude-config/issues/29/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sh4i-yurei/claude-config/issues/29/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}]